~ start
On the way to the Mechanics Department, you notice the mage who taught you thalassomancy, Jeremiah. You haven't seen him since the Butterfly Courtyard, and decide to go say hello. 
~ Mid
- "You were a student here?"
	"Yeah, for the past year. Tuition isn't easy, but it's a lot less trouble than trying to research on your own." He shakes his head. => Mid
- "What's with... that?" \n You wave to the Mechanics Department ahead. 
	"Ah?" He looks back and forth between you and the strange aglommeration of shapes looming ahead. "Did you get access to the Clockwork Isle?" He sounds mildly amazed. 
	- "That doesn't look much like an airship..."
		"Oh, the Clockwork Isle is only an airship in that it flies, really." He considers for a moment. "Honestly, you'd likely understand it better than me. You've built clocks and stuff." => Mid
- "Want to buy some deep water?" 
	"Nah, but thanks for the offer." He waves a hand. "It's suprising how few places you can find it in the city, to be honest." => Mid
- "Good talk, catch you later." 
	"See you around." 
=> END